#25
The Sacred Grounds~
     The clearing continues into the mist where you see nothing around you 
except shadows and fog.  Wispy tendrils writhe in and around your feet as
you stand, trying to get your bearings.  The fresh smell of loam and earth
slides gently into your nose when you breathe in and you feel a sense of peace
wash over you as you exhale.  Suddenly the area is lit by a dim light that
springs into life from nowhere, fifteen feet above the forest floor.  You see
that you are walking in a small graveyard, where several chiseled tombstones
mark those cherished faithful of Garou's who gave their lives for his cause.
The workmanship on the headstones is masterful, and the solemn atmosphere of 
this second clearing makes you humbly think of your own mortality, or 
immortality, as the case may be.
~
